With the uniform compact-support convention of <a href="#lem:tower-supports" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="lem:tower-supports">21</a>, there are natural quasi-isomorphisms $$\label{eq:laurent-descent}
 \mathbf R\Gamma_c(Z_U,\mathcal O^\flat;\mathcal D)
       \simeq\mathscr W_{\mathcal D}[-r],
 \qquad
 \mathbf R\Gamma_c(Z_U,\mathcal O^\flat;\mathcal D)^{\varphi=1}
       \simeq W_{\mathcal D}[-r].$$ They are compatible with finite marking maps, the idempotent $e$, and the actions defined over $k$. The support cohomology is therefore concentrated in cohomological degree $r$, both before and after coefficient descent. Every fixed normalized root basis $b_1^{1/h},\ldots,b_N^{1/h}$ gives the same module and the same complete-step category.

outputs.exact_statement:
For every $s\geq0$ and every compact profinite $\mathcal D$, extension of constants induces natural quasi-isomorphisms $$\begin{aligned}
 E_{\mathcal D}\otimes_{\mathbb F_p}\mathbf R\Gamma_c(Y_s,\mathbb F_p)
   &\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }
       \mathbf R\Gamma_c(Y_s\times\underline{\mathcal D},\mathbb F_p),
       \label{eq:ind-fp-parameters}\\
 R_{\mathcal D}\otimes_{\mathbb F_p}\mathbf R\Gamma_c(Y_s,\mathbb F_p)
   &\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }
       \mathbf R\Gamma_c(Y_s\times\underline{\mathcal D},\mathcal O^\flat).
       \label{eq:ind-algebraic-comparison}
\end{aligned}$$ The tensors are algebraic. The comparisons retain uniform support and all compact bar parameters.*

*Each $H_c^i(Y_s,\mathbb F_p)$ is a countable smooth admissible $M_s$-module. It has a smooth commuting $P_m$-action. Smooth means that each vector has open stabilizer; admissible means that every open subgroup of $M_s$ has finite-dimensional fixed space.

With the uniform compact-support convention of <a href="#lem:tower-supports" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="lem:tower-supports">21</a>, there are natural quasi-isomorphisms $$\label{eq:laurent-descent}
 \mathbf R\Gamma_c(Z_U,\mathcal O^\flat;\mathcal D)
       \simeq\mathscr W_{\mathcal D}[-r],
 \qquad
 \mathbf R\Gamma_c(Z_U,\mathcal O^\flat;\mathcal D)^{\varphi=1}
       \simeq W_{\mathcal D}[-r].$$ They are compatible with finite marking maps, the idempotent $e$, and the actions defined over $k$. The support cohomology is therefore concentrated in cohomological degree $r$, both before and after coefficient descent. Every fixed normalized root basis $b_1^{1/h},\ldots,b_N^{1/h}$ gives the same module and the same complete-step category.

Fix the index $s$ and generator $e_s$ of <a href="#prop:pro-top-operation" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="prop:pro-top-operation">57</a>, and choose a generator $e'_0\in\operatorname{Ext}^d_\Lambda(k,k)$. There is one sufficiently deep marking subgroup $U_*$ such that for every allowed $q\geq s$ the composite $$\label{eq:pro-composite-extension}
 \mathsf N_s\longrightarrow\mathsf N_q
 \xrightarrow{\operatorname{Coind}_q(e'_0)}
 \mathsf N_q[d]\longrightarrow k[d]$$ equals a nonzero scalar multiple of $e_s$ in the equivariant Ext group for $T\rtimes U_*$. The first and last maps use the natural auxiliary actions, which are retained for every $q$.

For every prime $p$, every $n\geq1$, and every $j\in\mathbb Z$, the free rank is $$\label{eq:sphere-ranks}
 r_{p,n,j}
   =\#\left\{I\subseteq\{1,\ldots,n\}:
            \sum_{i\in I}(1-2i)=j\right\}.$$ Equivalently, these ranks are the graded dimensions of the exterior $\mathbb Q_p$-algebra on generators in degrees $-1,-3,\ldots,-(2n-1)$.
